  "numerical_failure": {
    "category": "convergence",
    "affected_api": "sklearn.linear_model._sgd_fast._plain_sgd",
    "observed_behavior": "SGD convergence check (early stopping with tol != None) uses only the loss term without regularization, so SGDOneClassSVM stops prematurely after about 6 epochs (initial epoch plus 5 for n_iter_no_change tolerance); the reported verbose 'Avg. loss' can reach 0.0 and then increase as the model converges.",
    "expected_behavior": "Convergence should be judged on the full optimization objective including regularization (and bias term), so training continues until the objective actually converges instead of stopping prematurely.",
    "manifestation": "wrong_value",
    "trigger_conditions": [
      "tol != None (early stopping / tolerance-based convergence enabled)",
      "SGDOneClassSVM or other SGD models using the default stopping criteria",
      "learning_rate not PA1 or PA2",
      "penalty_type > 0 (regularization enabled) for the regularization term to be included"
    ],
    "input_output_examples": [
      {
        "input": "SGDOneClassSVM with default stopping criteria on a higher-dimensional dataset",
        "buggy_output": "Training stops after about 6 epochs (Avg. loss reported near 0.0 and then increasing)",
        "expected_output": "Training continues until the objective converges (not stopped after 6 epochs)",
        "value_kind": "count",
        "source": "issue#30027"
      }
    ],
    "oracle_clues": [
      "test_sgd_oneclass_convergence() should fail on main and succeed with the PR",
      "verbose output reports Objective alongside Avg. loss after the fix",
      "changelog states output of SGD models can change for tol != None"
    ]
  },
  "numerical_characteristics": {
    "dtype": null,
    "precision": null,
    "magnitude": null,
    "tolerance": "tol=1e-3 in the regression test test_sgd_oneclass_convergence; tol=None with manual max_iter cap is the suggested workaround; reference OneClassSVM uses tol=1e-6 in test_sgd_oneclass_vs_linear_oneclass",
    "category_specific_evidence": [
      "Issue #30027: SGDOneClassSVM stops prematurely because the stopping criterion uses the raw error/loss (which can be 0.0 and then increase) rather than the full objective including regularization and the bias term.",
      "Optimization almost always stops after 6 epochs (initial epoch plus 5 for the stopping tolerance); the number of epochs for the stopping tolerance cannot be changed.",
      "Problem does not manifest with toy (low-dimensional) data because 6 epochs is likely enough there.",
      "Actual output shows Avg. loss values around 0.000088-0.000267 over epochs 1-5 for 10k samples, 10 features, with Bias changing each epoch.",
      "PR #31856 changes the stopping criterion to the full objective (with regularization, and intercept term for one-class SVM) and accumulates L1 norm in WeightVector.",
      "Regression test test_sgd_oneclass_convergence uses nu in [0.1, 0.5, 0.9], max_iter=100, tol=1e-3, learning_rate='constant', eta0=1e-3 and asserts n_iter_ > 6.",
      "Test test_sgd_oneclass_vs_linear_oneclass compares SGDOneClassSVM (max_iter=20000, tol=None, eta0=1e-3) with liblinear OneClassSVM(kernel='linear', tol=1e-6) on iris data.",
      "Commit history notes a test was made to converge by setting tol=None."
    ],
    "reproduction_risks": [
      "The initial epoch plus five stopping-tolerance epochs means the premature stop appears around epoch 6, so reproduction must run past that with the default tol.",
      "Behaviour is not reproduced on small, low-dimensional toy data; use a higher-dimensional dataset (e.g. 10k samples, 1000 features as in the PR example).",
      "Changing tol to None with a manual max_iter is a workaround that slows optimisation and is not the fix itself.",
      "The passages do not state the dtype or the precision used in the bug run.",
      "The exact magnitude regime of the input features is not given in the passages."
    ]
  },
